## Commands

```bash
npm install        # setup
npm run build      # tsdown, outputs to dist/
npm run dev        # tsdown --watch
npm test           # vitest run --passWithNoTests
npm run typecheck  # tsc --noEmit
npm run fix        # ultracite fix: format + lint autofix
npm run check      # ultracite check (CI)
```

## Gotchas

- ESM only, NodeNext: relative imports need `.js` extensions even from `.ts` sources.
- Two build entries: `cli.js` (shebang, no types) and `index.js` (types). Do not merge them, and do not add a shebang to `src/cli.ts`.
- Lint and format through `npm run fix` and `npm run check`, not oxlint or oxfmt directly.
- Colors via `styleText` from `node:util`; progress via the `@clack/prompts` spinner. No chalk or ora.

## Agent invariants

- Data on stdout; logs and progress on stderr. `--output json` for machine-readable output.
- Never prompts when stdin is not a TTY; `--no-input` plus flags for every value.
- Mutating commands support `--dry-run`; destructive ones require `--yes` without a TTY.
- In `--output json` mode, errors print `{ error, code, message, details }` on stdout and exit non-zero.
- Core logic lives in `src/index.ts` so it can back an MCP server too; CLI-only concerns stay in `src/cli.ts`.
